                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0342593b-1382-44e1-b878-19e1bdf6b796",
                        "source_entry_id": "a860d875-0e91-38bb-894f-6e290c452231",
                        "source_sense_id": "e7b6442c-af5d-359d-946a-f269fb65c5ff",
                        "source_sense_description": "plek van enorm verdriet",
                        "target_lang_word": "Jammertal",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Jammertal",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fd984c1c-c349-36e6-85e4-6fb45ffd64db",
                                        "entry_id": "5b4ea175-ec96-3956-9424-ea5115269ba0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "das Leben auf der Erde, im Gegensatz zum Himmel"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d26c40db-9c1c-4d5d-b67e-348584715a02",
                                                "sense_id": "fd984c1c-c349-36e6-85e4-6fb45ffd64db",
                                                "text": "„Man kann im Parsifal aber auch den Blick nach unten richten ins irdische Jammertal der Gralsritter, auf ihr Leiden an Liebesmangel und Entbehrungen und den allgegenwärtigen Schmerz, den die Sündenwunden bereiten.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e115156c-5260-4009-8828-43926ded6c50",
                                                "sense_id": "fd984c1c-c349-36e6-85e4-6fb45ffd64db",
                                                "text": "„Bodendiek sieht im Augenblick nicht so aus, als könne er das Jammertal nicht ertragen.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8346151d-7d4c-326d-8ee2-c0f4db17a675",
                                        "entry_id": "5b4ea175-ec96-3956-9424-ea5115269ba0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Zustand, der traurig oder allgemein sehr schlecht ist"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figurative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "40c47d41-a656-4670-8557-6d03fb2b46a5",
                                                "sense_id": "8346151d-7d4c-326d-8ee2-c0f4db17a675",
                                                "text": "„Deutschland ist auf dem Weg aus dem Jammertal, die Binnenkonjunktur springt wieder an.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "35c034c5-7a2e-4446-b2c5-dd6392862f36",
                                                "sense_id": "8346151d-7d4c-326d-8ee2-c0f4db17a675",
                                                "text": "„Der allgegenwärtige Beschallungsmüll in den Konsumtempeln lehrt, selbst besinnliche Melodien zu verabscheuen. Tröstlich, dass es inmitten dieses vorweihnachtlichen Jammertals die ordnende Hand der MA 48 gibt.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ec720922-b912-4b77-acd0-cacfcd826ccb",
                                                "sense_id": "8346151d-7d4c-326d-8ee2-c0f4db17a675",
                                                "text": "„Alle diese Vorgänge auf der Bundesebene schienen nicht geeignet zu sein, der Berliner FDP aus ihrem Jammertal zu helfen.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c7812fef-2e93-40d0-b6f8-aa92bb8d456a",
                        "source_entry_id": "a860d875-0e91-38bb-894f-6e290c452231",
                        "source_sense_id": "e7b6442c-af5d-359d-946a-f269fb65c5ff",
                        "source_sense_description": "plek van enorm verdriet",
                        "target_lang_word": "vale of tears",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "vale of tears",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fb29ac57-a40f-3c19-890c-1b106e5eee64",
                                        "entry_id": "f849582a-327f-3bda-820e-c3bfc7ec584c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The world, a place where difficulties and the sorrows of life are felt, especially (Christianity) as a place to be left behind when one dies and goes to heaven."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "idiomatic",
                                            "literary",
                                            "often",
                                            "poetic",
                                            "singular"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b8dd4c39-4006-4538-9969-f321d678d610",
                                                "sense_id": "fb29ac57-a40f-3c19-890c-1b106e5eee64",
                                                "text": "He [Vitus Theodorus] was called to be a Paſtor at Norinberg, his own country, [...] till it pleaſed God to put an end to his labors, by tranſlating him out of this vale of tears into his Everlaſting Kingdom, Anno Chriſti 1549."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dedbcea0-852e-46bb-9951-fb6a09fc0145",
                                                "sense_id": "fb29ac57-a40f-3c19-890c-1b106e5eee64",
                                                "text": "While we ſojourn in this vale of Tears and Sorrow, we are detain'd from the bleſſ'd Sight and Enjoyment of God; and kept from the Happineſs of juſt Men made perfect."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "01380721-34dd-44db-90e9-0f96f80676de",
                                                "sense_id": "fb29ac57-a40f-3c19-890c-1b106e5eee64",
                                                "text": "But let us recommend all to god, who alone know what ſhall befal in this vale of tears, this evil world we have here, in which there is ſcarce any thing to be found without ſome mixture of iniquity, impoſture, or knavery."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "170e98ab-8b4a-4b42-a22b-4fe7db54d15f",
                                                "sense_id": "fb29ac57-a40f-3c19-890c-1b106e5eee64",
                                                "text": "Body o' me, it makes a man sick of his kind, ashamed to belong to the race of men, to see the envy that abounds in this here sublunary wale^([sic – meaning vale]) of tears!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d641a8f6-2279-44e8-93a6-9ed92eaa28bb",
                                                "sense_id": "fb29ac57-a40f-3c19-890c-1b106e5eee64",
                                                "text": "We must not call earth a vale of tears. It is neither pious to do so, nor in any respect proper. We might as well, nay, with far greater propriety, call it a field of laughter."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ec061fec-a6be-4976-9904-f43dc4be17fe",
                                                "sense_id": "fb29ac57-a40f-3c19-890c-1b106e5eee64",
                                                "text": "I excused myself and dropped to the rear of the procession, sad at heart, willing to go hence from this troubled life, this vale of tears, this brief day of broken rest, of cloud and storm, of weary struggle and monotonous defeat; and yet shrinking from the change, as remembering how long eternity is, and how many have wended thither who know that anecdote."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b0bef333-c4af-489d-a0f7-34c25f9201d0",
                                                "sense_id": "fb29ac57-a40f-3c19-890c-1b106e5eee64",
                                                "text": "Driven by such a hope, as if refusing to recognize this world as a vale of tears where (as they taught me) even injustice is foreordained by Providence to maintain the balance of things, whose design often eludes us, Salvatore journeyed through various lands, from his native Montferrat toward Liguria, then up through Provence into the lands of the King of France."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b9166e1e-dc31-4812-b23e-fb65d322e013",
                                                "sense_id": "fb29ac57-a40f-3c19-890c-1b106e5eee64",
                                                "text": "So it was steady as she goes as Sally was hustled into bed, and on the stroke of twelve a fourth Aintree child entered this vale of tears."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a447799b-3b6f-4978-bd3d-bbce9e9ea4d6",
                                                "sense_id": "fb29ac57-a40f-3c19-890c-1b106e5eee64",
                                                "text": "As we devour the Earth's resources and despoil the environment, we are driving ourselves into a metaphoric vale of tears."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ccadf01d-ef7a-3270-8ff1-ede2cf30c190",
                                        "entry_id": "f849582a-327f-3bda-820e-c3bfc7ec584c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A particular place of sorrow or suffering."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "idiomatic",
                                            "literary",
                                            "often",
                                            "poetic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6f4c7a24-decc-44bd-81cb-66074217209f",
                                                "sense_id": "ccadf01d-ef7a-3270-8ff1-ede2cf30c190",
                                                "text": "That, in this pilgrimage of ſeventy years, / O'er rocks of perils, and through vales of tears, / Deſtin'd to march, our doubtful ſteps we tend, / Tir'd with the toil, yet fearful of its end: [...]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "29bcac3d-1fec-4843-a2bc-3d092e2133bb",
                                                "sense_id": "ccadf01d-ef7a-3270-8ff1-ede2cf30c190",
                                                "text": "If, friendleſs, in a vale of tears I ſtray, / Where briers wound, and thorns perplex my way, / Still let my ſteady ſoul thy goodneſs ſee, / And with ſtrong confidence lay hold on thee; [...]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c121d028-7574-4882-9f44-35def9dc6926",
                                                "sense_id": "ccadf01d-ef7a-3270-8ff1-ede2cf30c190",
                                                "text": "But though life's valley be a vale of tears, / A brighter ſcene beyond that vale appears, / Whoſe glory with a light that never fades, / Shoots between ſcattered rocks and opening ſhades, / And while it ſhows the land the ſoul deſires, / The language of the land ſhe ſeeks, inſpires."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a4b9c766-2189-4258-b77d-7717a80c08ab",
                                                "sense_id": "ccadf01d-ef7a-3270-8ff1-ede2cf30c190",
                                                "text": "Jerusalem is the city of tombs; the valleys of Halcedoma and Jehoshephat are covered with them; and the living appear to have no other task assigned to them than that of keeping watch over these deposits of ashes. [...] Such are these places of lamentations—these vales of tears—these vast repositories of death."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ddb01248-ec8c-4867-be14-2f129ef29d4d",
                                                "sense_id": "ccadf01d-ef7a-3270-8ff1-ede2cf30c190",
                                                "text": "[I]n the New World, Christianity had provided the major vehicle of cultural expression for the slaves. It could not be denied them in a Christian country—and it provided them with solace in their \"vale of tears,\" guiding them through \"the valley of the shadow.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1430e532-5e63-4c5b-bd68-4522b41bbdc6",
